WEBVTT

NOTE Animated terminal (1280x720, dark slate) showing the Vectify CLI workflow:
inspect the palette, trace, reduce to two colours, dump the pipeline stages, and
serve over HTTP. Cues are timed to the line animations in demo.svg.

00:00.900 --> 00:01.300
Command: vectify info logo.png

00:01.500 --> 00:02.100
Output: 500 by 129 pixels, palette of 8 colours

00:02.500 --> 00:02.900
Output: three swatches shown, each with its pixel population

00:03.300 --> 00:04.100
Note: index 0 is the lightest, so it becomes the background

00:04.100 --> 00:04.900
Command: vectify logo.png logo.svg

00:04.900 --> 00:05.700
Output: 8 colours, 7148 bytes of SVG

00:05.700 --> 00:06.500
Command: vectify logo.png logo.svg --colors 2

00:06.500 --> 00:07.300
Output: 2 colours, 2973 bytes of SVG

00:07.300 --> 00:08.100
Command: vectify logo.png out.svg --debug-dir ./trace

00:08.100 --> 00:08.500
Output: debug stages written to ./trace

00:08.500 --> 00:09.500
Files: 01-quantized, 02-regions, 03-curves, 04-curves.svg

00:09.500 --> 00:10.300
Command: vectify serve

00:10.300 --> 00:11.100
Output: serving on http://127.0.0.1:8080

00:11.100 --> 00:14.800
Routes: POST /vectify, GET /health, GET /info. Blank prompt.